01:47:27.266 --> 01:47:33.266
We decided that it was time for
Gmail to have add-on capability

01:47:33.266 --> 01:47:38.233
because people were wasting
simply too much time going from

01:47:38.233 --> 01:47:42.399
their primary work surface,
which could be Gmail, digressing

01:47:42.399 --> 01:47:45.899
over to a distraction, and then
by the time they come back 20

01:47:45.899 --> 01:47:48.600
minutes are gone.

01:47:48.600 --> 01:47:52.766
Rather than my doing the talking
and explaining this, I'm going

01:47:52.766 --> 01:47:58.300
to bring on stage a partner,
Intuit, who will explain what

01:47:58.300 --> 01:48:00.166
they did with Gmail add-ons.

01:48:00.166 --> 01:48:04.366
Please welcome to the
stage EVP and CTO of Inuit,

01:48:04.366 --> 01:48:05.633
Tayloe Stansbury.

01:48:15.966 --> 01:48:17.133
Welcome, Tayloe.

01:48:17.133 --> 01:48:17.766
Take it away.

01:48:18.333 --> 01:48:19.366
&gt;&gt; TAYLOE STANSBURY:
Thank you, Prabhaker.

01:48:19.366 --> 01:48:20.833
And good morning, everyone.

01:48:20.833 --> 01:48:21.866
I am delighted to be here.

01:48:22.833 --> 01:48:25.266
If I could just say a word or
two about Intuit, our primary

01:48:25.266 --> 01:48:28.466
brands are
TurboTax and QuickBooks.

01:48:28.466 --> 01:48:32.733
And with QuickBooks, we have
some 1.8 million online and

01:48:32.733 --> 01:48:35.333
mobile users around the world.

01:48:35.333 --> 01:48:39.433
Now it turns out that about a
half million of those users also

01:48:39.433 --> 01:48:40.966
use Gmail.

01:48:40.966 --> 01:48:44.366
It seemed natural that with this
add-on capability we would want

01:48:44.366 --> 01:48:47.933
to integrate the two so that
those users could have a more

01:48:47.933 --> 01:48:50.633
smooth flow between
those applications.

01:48:52.866 --> 01:48:55.066
So let me give an example.

01:48:55.066 --> 01:48:56.966
Here we have a
customer whose name is Craig.

01:48:56.966 --> 01:48:58.100
He's a gardener.

01:48:58.100 --> 01:49:00.600
He really loves making
people's gardens beautiful.

01:49:00.600 --> 01:49:03.133
And he's sitting in a cafe and
he's reading his Gmail on his

01:49:03.133 --> 01:49:06.866
phone and up comes a message
from his customer Sarah who says

01:49:06.866 --> 01:49:10.966
she's delighted with the work
that he's done on her garden and

01:49:10.966 --> 01:49:14.133
she's wondering how
she should pay him.

01:49:14.133 --> 01:49:17.800
He's thinking, wow, this is an
opportune time to invoice her.

01:49:17.800 --> 01:49:20.633
Now what it used to be is that
he would have to jump out of

01:49:20.633 --> 01:49:24.800
Gmail, go into QuickBooks,
log in, find the place to do

01:49:24.800 --> 01:49:25.466
an invoice.

01:49:26.066 --> 01:49:29.699
But instead what we did with
this add-on integration is that

01:49:29.699 --> 01:49:33.066
we have a QB icon that is
at the bottom of his Gmail.

01:49:33.066 --> 01:49:38.266
He simply clicks on that, it
infers context, single signs him

01:49:38.266 --> 01:49:41.866
on to QuickBooks, drops him
right into the place where he

01:49:41.866 --> 01:49:43.866
can fill out an invoice.

01:49:43.866 --> 01:49:47.199
And as you can see, it is
excerpted from the email the

01:49:47.199 --> 01:49:49.500
name and address
of his customer.

01:49:49.500 --> 01:49:52.866
Now all he has to do is fill in
the rest of the details for his

01:49:52.866 --> 01:49:55.899
invoice and off he goes.

01:49:55.899 --> 01:49:58.433
Remember, he's still in Gmail.

01:49:58.433 --> 01:50:01.866
He's never left the application
and he's been able to fill out

01:50:01.866 --> 01:50:03.833
the invoice entirely in there.

01:50:03.833 --> 01:50:06.366
Boom. He sends
the invoice and he's done.

01:50:06.366 --> 01:50:07.100
It was that easy.

01:50:09.566 --> 01:50:13.600
Now when he's done with that, he
can actually quickly look at how

01:50:13.600 --> 01:50:16.699
his invoices are doing with his
other customers in QuickBooks

01:50:16.699 --> 01:50:20.600
still inside the Gmail app, see
how that's going, and get right

01:50:20.600 --> 01:50:23.933
back into Gmail so he can finish
his coffee and go off to make

01:50:23.933 --> 01:50:25.733
other people's lawns beautiful.

01:50:26.800 --> 01:50:31.866
So, to summarize, it was really
easy to do this integration.

01:50:31.866 --> 01:50:35.800
We wrote once and deploy
many across Android, iOS,

01:50:35.800 --> 01:50:37.500
and the Web.

01:50:37.500 --> 01:50:39.133
We can't wait to
get this to market.

01:50:39.133 --> 01:50:41.166
It will be later this year.

01:50:41.166 --> 01:50:43.699
And this is just one of many
integrations that we expect to

01:50:43.699 --> 01:50:46.866
do between
QuickBooks and the G Suite.

01:50:46.866 --> 01:50:50.800
We already announced one earlier
around the calendar and we

01:50:50.800 --> 01:50:52.399
expect to have more over time.

01:50:52.399 --> 01:50:53.199
Thank you.

